.TH MATRIXCODE 6x "10 August 2026" "MatrixCode 0.2" "XScreenSaver manual"
.SH NAME
matrixcode \- original-era Matrix-style code rain with optional CRT treatment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B matrixcode
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B matrixcode
renders a fixed grid of original clean-room glyphs whose illumination moves
downward in independently timed waves.  The default operator1999 profile uses a
4:3 aperture and restrained CRT emulation to resemble photographed late-1990s
workstation displays rather than a generic full-screen neon text effect.
Window-size changes rebuild the simulation and restart animation timing so the
new drawable is filled immediately at the same logical composition.
.SH STARTUP SCENES
.TP
.B -scene neo-terminal
Play the Neo terminal takeover recreation before entering Matrix rain.  This is
the default.
.TP
.B -no-scene
Skip the startup scene and begin Matrix rain immediately.
.PP
Scenes are authored in a canonical 640x480 coordinate system and scale
uniformly to the target drawable.  Resizing restarts the presentation from the
beginning of the startup scene.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B -profile operator1999
Default.  80x60 reference density at 4:3, automatically extended with more
columns on wider targets, flat luminous rain bodies, bright cursors, and CRT
treatment.  Glyph pixel size is derived from target height.
.TP
.B -profile opening1999
Cleaner cinematic presentation without CRT treatment.
.TP
.B -profile clean
Neutral modern rendering for comparison and low-cost operation.
.SH GEOMETRY AND RAIN
.TP
.BI -columns " N"
4:3 reference columns, 40 to 240.  Default 80.  Lower values produce larger glyphs; auto aspect may add columns to fill wider targets.
.TP
.BI -aspect " auto|4:3|16:9|2.39:1"
Frame the code independently of the physical desktop aspect.
.TP
.BI -density " N"
Illuminated fraction of the rain cycle, 10 to 90.
.TP
.BI -speed " N"
Fall-speed percentage, 25 to 250.  The operator default is 40.
.TP
.BI -trail " N"
Rain period / luminous-run control, 6 to 40.
.TP
.BI -cycle " N"
Independent glyph-cycling rate, 0 to 300.
.TP
.BI -glow " N"
Optical glow strength, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI -contrast " N"
Ordinary-code brightness control, 20 to 100.
.SH CRT OPTIONS
.TP
.B -crt, -no-crt
Enable or disable CRT treatment.
.TP
.BI -curvature " N"
Tube curvature, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI -scanlines " N"
Scanline strength, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI -phosphor-mask " N"
Vertical phosphor-grille strength, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI -vignette " N"
Edge darkening, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI -persistence " N"
Phosphor after-image strength, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI -overscan " N"
Inset the simulated raster by 0 to 10 percent.
.SH XSCREENSAVER OPTIONS
.TP
.B -root
Draw into the root window.
.TP
.B -window
Create a preview window.
.TP
.BI -window-id " ID"
Draw into an existing X window.  XSCREENSAVER_WINDOW is also honored; this is
how XScreenSaver supplies one target window per physical monitor.
.TP
.BI -geometry " WxH"
Preview-window geometry.
.SH TIMING AND TESTING
.TP
.BI -fps " N"
Frame cap, 5 to 120.
.TP
.BI -delay " usec"
Frame delay in microseconds.
.TP
.BI -seed " N"
Use deterministic pseudo-random state.
.TP
.BI -frames " N"
Exit after exactly N rendered frames.
.TP
.BI -screenshot " FILE.ppm"
Capture the final frame as binary PPM.
.TP
.B -self-test
Run non-graphical internal tests.
.TP
.B -verbose
Print GL and grid diagnostics.
.SH COPYRIGHT
MIT/X11 licensed.  This unofficial project is unaffiliated with the owners of
The Matrix and contains no extracted film assets or official font data.
